4- View order history (Gianfranco)

ID:
UC-PRC-04
Title:
View order history
Description:
An authenticated user views the order history permitted by their role. Billing information is displayed only where authorized.
Primary Actor:
Customer, Restaurant Owner/Staff, Courier or Platform Operator
Preconditions:
The user is authenticated and has one of the supported roles.
Postconditions:
The permitted history is displayed. Orders and ledger entries remain unchanged.
Inputs:
Authenticated user identity and role, including their associated restaurant or courier profile where applicable.
Outputs:
Authorized order records, final states and timestamps, together with permitted charges and separate refund entries. Couriers do not receive customer payment details.
Main Success Scenario:
  The user opens the order history view.
The system identifies the authenticated user and their role.
The system determines the permitted records: the customer’s own orders, the restaurant’s own orders, the courier’s deliveries, or all orders for the platform operator.
The system retrieves the records within that scope.
The system displays the authorized history and permitted billing information.
For refunded orders, the system displays the refund as a separate entry while preserving the original charge for users authorized to view billing records.











